From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:51:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(txe): choose where bb, the world state and the AVM run
 when the TXE starts

The TXE's backends (wasm, process or napi) are now one choice made at setup, the
bin's --backends flag (default wasm), passed to the dispatcher, every worker and
each session, instead of TXE_WORLD_STATE for the world state and the AVM and wasm
hard-wired for bb. Each thread seeds its bb.js singletons with the same choice:
wasm modules; a bb process (BarretenbergSync over shared memory, Barretenberg over
a unix socket); or instances of bb's shared library (on the calling thread, and on
a worker thread of their own).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

